# The server's address, written once.
#
# Four deployment files carry it -- nginx's server_name and certificate,
# Keycloak's KC_HOSTNAME, the realm's redirect URIs, ShinyProxy's OIDC
# endpoints -- and they have to agree. deploy/scripts/render.sh reads
# this file and writes all four from their .template neighbours.
#
#   cp deploy/host.env.template deploy/host.env
#   $EDITOR deploy/host.env
#   deploy/scripts/render.sh
#
# host.env is gitignored and excluded from the rsync in the README: it
# describes your server, not the software.
#
# An IP address or a DNS name, exactly as users will type it into the
# browser and as the TLS certificate's subjectAltName carries it. No
# scheme, no port, no path.
OMICSAPP_HOST=REPLACE_ME

# Who may reach the administrative endpoints through nginx: Keycloak's
# admin console (/auth/admin), its master realm, and ShinyProxy's admin
# page. Everyone else gets 403; users never need them. IPv4/IPv6
# addresses or CIDRs, space-separated, e.g. "127.0.0.1 ::1 203.0.113.25".
# Empty means the server itself: 127.0.0.1, ::1 and OMICSAPP_HOST.
# Re-run render.sh and re-copy the nginx site after changing it.
ADMIN_ALLOW_CIDR=

# Addresses nginx's rate limits do not count (see "Security headers and
# rate limits" in deploy/README.md). Same form as above. Empty means the
# server itself -- which must be on the list, because ShinyProxy fetches
# every user's sign-in tokens from Keycloak through nginx from there.
# Add a reverse proxy or NAT gateway here only if every user arrives
# through it, and know that it then exempts all of them.
RATE_LIMIT_EXEMPT_CIDR=
